---
name: smoke-tests

description: |
  Errand verifying RustFS cluster is healthy and S3 API functions end-to-end.
  Probes /health on every peer discovered via the rustfs-peer BOSH link, then
  performs a full S3 cycle — CreateBucket, PutObject, GetObject (content verify),
  DeleteObject, HeadObject (expect 404), DeleteBucket — against the first peer.

  Authentication uses AWS Signature Version 2 via openssl + curl. No extra
  packages are required beyond the Ubuntu Noble stemcell base tools (bash, curl,
  openssl, base64, date).

  Packages block is intentionally empty for v0.1. When a bundled mc or aws-cli
  blob package is added, list it here and update templates/bin/run.erb accordingly.

packages: []

templates:
  bin/run.erb: bin/run

consumes:
  - name: rustfs-peer
    type: rustfs-peer

properties:
  rustfs.access_key:
    description: |
      Admin access key for smoke-test S3 operations.
      Must match the rustfs.access_key set on the rustfs-server job.

  rustfs.secret_key:
    description: |
      Admin secret key for smoke-test S3 operations.
      Must match the rustfs.secret_key set on the rustfs-server job.

  rustfs.port:
    description: S3 API port. Must match the rustfs-server job's rustfs.port.
    default: 9000

  rustfs.region:
    description: |
      S3 region string to present in API requests.
      Must match the rustfs-server job's rustfs.region.
    default: us-east-1

  rustfs.tls.certificate:
    description: |
      API TLS certificate of the rustfs-server job. Used only as a signal:
      when non-empty the errand probes endpoints over https (verification is
      skipped with -k, so no key or CA is required here). Leave unset for a
      plaintext http cluster. Must mirror the rustfs-server job's
      rustfs.tls.certificate.
    default: ""

  smoke_tests.timeout_secs:
    description: curl --max-time value in seconds for each request.
    default: 30
